variables: []
role: llm.format.toon
response_format: text
---
The data below is encoded in TOON (Token-Oriented Object Notation), a compact
indentation-based format. Read it like this:

- `key: value` is a field. The value is plain text; `true`, `false`, `null`
  and numbers are literals.
- `key[N]:` introduces a list of N items. Every item starts with `- `.
- `key[N]: a,b` is an inline list of N scalar values; `key: []` is an empty
  list.
- A nested object is a `key:` line followed by an indented block of fields.
- Two spaces of indentation per level show the nesting. Objects have no
  braces and no brackets.

Example:

[2]:
  - title: Introduction
    tags[2]: a,b
    score: 0.5
  - title: Background
    tags: []
    score: 0.9
